{
  "abstract": "A known rational almost septuple has five regular quadruples covering twenty of its twenty-one pairwise square conditions. We study all ordinary markings of these five quadruples, allowing the two regular-quintuple relations of the known example to vary. The two regular fourths of a companion triple give a natural difference parameter, $\\delta=D+E-C$. For every rational value of this parameter the markings project with finite fibres to a geometrically irreducible curve of genus 31. Thus each fixed difference has finitely many rational markings, with the uncovered edge allowed to have a nonsquare radicand. A signed trace inverse also gives at most 24 terminal entries over any fixed pair of marked entries. We prove constancy of the genus on the complement of a branch-collision locus and determine all thirteen rational collision values by exact elimination. Characteristic-zero normalization gives the same genus at each exceptional value. On the fibre through the known example a second rational point has all twenty-one square roots, a repeated entry and a zero entry. A nonzero Jacobian determinant and a transverse derivative separate these entries over the reals and every p-adic field while keeping the difference fixed. The rational point sets of the fixed fibres and the global septuple problem remain open.",
